Workers without each other's channels

As it starts a worker, the master passes the new worker's channel, a
socket, to every other worker with SCM_RIGHTS, so that workers could
write to each other. Radix sends no socket to another process, as a
socket sent over its own connection could keep itself open, and answers
EOPNOTSUPP. nginx's workers never write to each other: only the master
writes to a worker's channel. So a channel that cannot be passed is left
out, with a debug line rather than an alert at each worker's start.

diff --git a/src/os/unix/ngx_channel.c b/src/os/unix/ngx_channel.c
index b03bbbb..e450025 100644
--- a/src/os/unix/ngx_channel.c
+++ b/src/os/unix/ngx_channel.c
@@ -84,6 +84,22 @@ ngx_write_channel(ngx_socket_t s, ngx_channel_t *ch, size_t size,
             return NGX_AGAIN;
         }
 
+#if (NGX_HAVE_MSGHDR_MSG_CONTROL)
+
+        /*
+         * Radix sends no socket to another process (Dukovo's patch), so
+         * a worker goes without the channels of the others, which only
+         * the master writes to.
+         */
+
+        if (err == NGX_EOPNOTSUPP && ch->fd != -1) {
+            ngx_log_debug1(NGX_LOG_DEBUG_CORE, log, err,
+                           "channel %d not passed", ch->fd);
+            return NGX_DECLINED;
+        }
+
+#endif
+
         ngx_log_error(NGX_LOG_ALERT, log, err, "sendmsg() failed");
         return NGX_ERROR;
     }
